From: Linux Fieldwork <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] depmod: execute from ToolsTree against the target root

`run_depmod()` currently uses `chroot_cmd(root=context.rootoptions)`. That
makes the executable come from the target image and, on the affected path,
leaves lookup sensitive to the invoking host's PATH. In particular, a
ToolsTree with `/usr/sbin/depmod` still fails when the host PATH omits
`/usr/sbin`.

Run depmod through `Context.sandbox()` so executable lookup uses the
configured ToolsTree. Bind the image at `/buildroot` and use depmod's
`--basedir` option for all module input and generated metadata.

This keeps operation ownership explicit:

- executable and libraries: ToolsTree;
- module tree and generated metadata: target image at `/buildroot`.

Closes the failure mode described by systemd/mkosi#4319.
---
 mkosi/__init__.py | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mkosi/__init__.py b/mkosi/__init__.py
index 9e35c53..0000000 100644
--- a/mkosi/__init__.py
+++ b/mkosi/__init__.py
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
@@
-        with complete_step(f"Running depmod for {modulesd.name}"):
-            run(["depmod", "--all", modulesd.name], sandbox=chroot_cmd(root=context.rootoptions))
+        with complete_step(f"Running depmod for {modulesd.name}"):
+            run(
+                ["depmod", "--basedir", "/buildroot", "--all", modulesd.name],
+                sandbox=context.sandbox(options=context.rootoptions()),
+            )
-- 
